# Knowledge

Format: `K###: <finding|decision|gotcha> [verified|partial|unverified|stale] (N###; path) {cites:n}`.
K ids assigned at lint 2026-11-09; results paths are under `.agent-research/results/`.

## Headline
- K030: GOAL RE-BASED TO v10 LABELS (N051, user decision 2026-11-17): per-marker asinh cofactor by a pre-registered label-only rule (CD123/CD14/CD19/CD3/CD56/HLA-DR 500, CD16/CD45 150). On v10: N031 .6703 (was .6527 on v5; re-base), N048 (trained on cofactor-150 labels) .6804 = new best (+.0101 > 2 x noise), v10-trained .6788; in-distribution reference .6862. Training on cleaner labels helps only when scored on cleaner labels (frozen-v5 flat). Correction: cofactor 150/500 does NOT erase CD123+ cells (tail contrast 49.5 -> 68.7/76.3); the N049 d'=0 fit was a local optimum [verified] (N048, N051; .agent-research/results/N051-label-v10-per-marker-asinh-cofactor-pre/n051_retrain_goal.csv) {cites:0}
- K029: LABEL COFACTOR ERROR (N047, reproduced): v3-v5 single labels = asinh(x / q10_slide); for dim dyes q10 is tiny (CD3 .06-.84, CD56 .17-1.59) and asinh amplifies negative-cell noise. Fixed cofactor 50: CD3 r of the SAME N031 predictions .53->.78 / .60->.77, CD56 .26->.37 / .30->.46, FOV excess CD3 .49->.12; other markers unchanged; N031 ensemble would read .683 on such labels (re-base, not progress). FOV offsets are not image-visible (R^2 <= .03); the draw-2 gap is a draw-specific readout (autofl slope flips sign between draws); GOAL-family members share errors (residual r .95-.97) [verified] (N047; .agent-research/results/N047-review-2-lf-mk-goal-6527-target-67-after/d2_cofactor_check.csv) {cites:0}
- K028: GOAL IS CAPPED BY FOV-LEVEL LABEL ERROR (N038): scored within fields of view the N031 ensemble reaches .7211 vs pooled .6527 (CD19 .30->.48/.40->.63, CD56 .38->.56/.36->.53, CD3 .56->.77/.60->.74); CD19/CD56/CD3 v5 labels carry FOV-level variance .34-.49 above a permutation null while LF predictions carry ~0; cause = the authors' smoothed background_lowess in the dim dye channel shared by CD3/CD19/CD56 (per-cell background: FOV excess ~.03). The '.658 in-distribution ceiling' was a confounded comparison (N022 tail05 FOV .680, gain only in-distribution). Clean ceiling N039: v5-trained r50 that sees both draws .678 on the GOAL cells (data-matched 128k .659) vs held-out base .643; the shift cost sits in train-draw-0 -> test-draw-1 (.034; HLA-DR + pooled targets), none in the other direction; per-cell background removes the offsets (v8: CD19 FOV excess .51 -> .00) but changes the labels (r .48-.70 with v5) and failed its QC. Low-pass 1.5 px input costs weak targets <= .011 (N042: not image-limited); label count 50 -> 100 % lifts weak targets +.035 (N040). Seed sd on v5 .0027 [verified] (N038; .agent-research/results/N038-review-lf-mk-common-11-batch-held-out-go/d2_within_fov.csv) {cites:0}
- K033: DENSE PSEUDO-LABELS (NOISY STUDENT) ARE THE ONLY MODEL-SIDE GAIN SINCE N031, SUB-THRESHOLD (N040, N046; scored on v5): label-count curve 25/50/100 % .6036/.6272/.6425 (weak4 .347/.396/.430); round-1 student ensemble .6564 vs N031 .6527 (+.0037 < 2 x noise, 16/22 items, p .0013), single student base .6529 vs .6425 (+.0103, 19/22); round 2 (teacher = student) .6546 does NOT compound (-.0018 vs round 1, confirmation bias); 4-model N040+N046 .6557 [verified] (N040, N046; .agent-research/results/N046-noisy-student-round-2-teacher-n040-stude/scores_goal.csv, .agent-research/results/N040-dense-label-completion-noisy-student-lab/n040_lc_per_target.csv) {cites:0}
- K019: LABEL QC (N023): batch-1 'all'-slide pooled CD123/HLA-DR/CD14 labels fail QC -- mono>lym contrast +1.21/+1.43 SD in batch 0 vs -.08/-.28 in batch 1 (LF-feature classes, SSL-only control agrees); released pooled value on CD16-only slides (no such antibody) exceeds the batch-1 'all' signal (q90 87.8 vs 41.9). Masked + per-slide z of multi-slide targets -> targets_v5. GOAL re-based to common-11 on v5 (same model .5742 legacy -> .6343; 90 % = dropping the failed target, NOT progress); training on v5 labels .6404 vs .6346 seed-matched (gain only where labels were repaired: b1to0 grp CD3/19/56 +.10, grp CD16 +.05) [verified] (N023; .agent-research/results/N023-label-qc-per-batch-dye-amplitude-single/) {cites:1}
- K025: CLINICAL TRANSFER IS TEACHER-RUN DEPENDENT (N032): MLL23 mean over 12 fine contrasts .611/.551/.493/.477 for four LF-teacher runs (student seeds inside each), mean .53; same-cell autofl truth is teacher-independent (.564-.570 / .843-.848). Robust across teachers: lineage contrasts (PBC .95-1.00; MLL23 segneut CD16 .92, mono CD14 .89), held-out PBC erythroblast CD45 .87, IG CD16 .80, MLL23 hairy HLA-DR .72, myelocyte CD16 .70; failing: NK/LGL CD56/CD16, basophil CD123, plasma/normoblast CD45, hairy CD19/CD3; eos CD16 teacher-dependent. Data engine (318k virtual-stained labelled cells, N033) flat (+.014 within noise). Report clinical numbers as means over >= 3 teacher runs [verified] (N032, N033; .agent-research/results/N032-teacher-run-variance-of-clinical-transfe/n032_n033_metrics.csv) {cites:1}
- K023: GOAL best .6515 = 2-model ensemble (full-view + 2x centre-zoom SSL-init r50; replicates .6512/.6518) vs single .6404, same-scale ensemble .6438, zoom+zoom .6491 (scale complementarity only +.002-.003). AdaBN hurts (-.005..-.011), no-maxpool hurts, shared-BN dual-scale collapses (BN confound). Giemsa student capacity is tuned: MLL23 fine .48/.59/.61/.53/.42 for 0/2/4/8/L trainable blocks. Inductive control N031 (SSL pretrained WITHOUT the held-out batch): ensemble .6527, base .6425, zoom2 .6442 -- no transductive inflation; GOAL now inductive, best .6527 (v5 metric; GOAL since re-based to v10, K030) [verified] (N026, N027, N030; .agent-research/results/N026-lf-teacher-resolution-test-time-batch-ad/goal_arms.csv) {cites:1}
- K011: GS student (distilled from the LF teacher) vs detrended autofl truth on the held-out stained slide: b0->b1 .648/.658 (2 seeds) vs teacher .559; b1->b0 .32 vs .31 (5.7k training cells). A better MARKER teacher (SSL r50) is worse on GS autofl (.40/.08) and leaves the student nearly unchanged (.641/.303) -> autofl cannot rank teachers for the marker task [verified] (N010, N015; N010-image-level-gs-encoder-dinobloom-b-last/gs_student_autofl_v4.csv, N015-gs-chain-with-the-ssl-init-r50-teacher-f/n015_measurements.csv) {cites:3}
- K001: BSCCM has NO cell with both Giemsa/Wright (G) and surface markers (M): all 15,712 histology cells are unstained. Label-free LED images (L) exist for all 412,941 cells and are the only bridge (G-L 15.7k pairs, L-M ~350k). G->M is transitive; validity rests on G ⊥ M | L (statistical-matching CIA) [verified] (N004; N001-bsccm-training-format-pack-fixed-record/audit.txt) {cites:4}
- K007: SLIDE-POSITION ARTEFACT in the fluorescence readouts: position alone (region-blocked GBM, median over slides) predicts autofl r .84, CD19 .84, CD56 .53, CD123 .49; CD16/CD14/CD45 nearly clean; LF features encode position (r .92). Labels detrended -> targets_v4; inputs keep real artefacts [verified] (N012, N013; N012-skeptic-control-is-the-within-slide-gs-a/spatial_detrend.json, N013-targets-v4-remove-slide-position-artefac/targets_v4_detrend_summary.csv) {cites:6}

## Topics

### Data and labels
- K002: Markers are partially observed (single-antibody cells = 1 marker; 37k 'all' cells = 4 spectral groups); cell-type gates only for 10,161 batch-0 'all' cells; no donor IDs (2 batches) [verified] (N004; N001-bsccm-training-format-pack-fixed-record/audit.txt) {cites:2}
- K003: Training format: /hnvme/workspace/v181bb10-bsccm/pack/*.npy fixed-record memmaps (row = global_index), targets*.npz (masked asinh(x/50) markers, gate classes, FOV split) [verified] (N001; /hnvme/workspace/v181bb10-bsccm/pack/) {cites:3}

### LF teacher
- K004: v3 LF->MK baseline (resnet18, 23 LED + phase): FOV .707 | batch-held-out .494/.471; signal mostly cell type (3-class oracle >= model on gated cells, CD16 .95 vs .88; within-class r .08-.45); CD19/CD56/CD123 collapse across batches. GOAL best .4835 -> superseded by K008/K010 (GOAL re-based on v4; the collapse was label artefact, K007) [verified] (N006; N006-supervised-lf-mk-baseline-on-curated-tar/n006v3_summary.csv, noise_seed_reruns.csv) {cites:3}
- K017: SSL LF encoders are weak as frozen linear probes (FOV .52 vs supervised .71; batch-held-out aug .486/.472 ~ supervised .491/.475, xillum worse .460/.435) but give the best teacher once fine-tuned (K010) [verified] (N007, N014; N007-ssl-pretraining-of-the-lf-encoder-cross/probe_batch_holdout.csv) {cites:2}
- K018: Adversarial domain invariance (DANN) is flat or harmful in every setting tried: GS slide (N010, .284-.308 all within noise), LF batch (N014, .5541 vs .5545), PBC unconditional (N020, unstable) and anchored (N021, harmful) [partial: N010 numbers only in the item text] (N010, N014, N020, N021; N014-teacher-v4-portfolio-resnet50-x15-ep-ssl/n014_goal.csv) {cites:4}
- K008: On v4 labels the LF teacher transfers across isolations: batch-held-out mean r .5545 (v3 .4835), FOV .635, FOV-vs-batch gap .22 -> .08; held-out CD19 -.05 -> .28/.32; seed noise .002 [verified] (N013; N013-targets-v4-remove-slide-position-artefac/n013_v4_noise.csv, n013_v4_final_evals.json) {cites:4}
- K031: LABEL-SIDE FIXES THAT DID NOT MOVE THE GOAL: cross-fitted position detrend (N036, v5cx: split-0 FOV-share gap .055 -> .017 = no-detrend level, residual held-out position signal ~ v5c; trend is real, out-of-fold explains autofl .824 vs in-sample .827) and the retrain on it (N037 ensemble .6537 vs .6527, +.0010 flat; test cells are all split 2 so were never in-sample detrended); per-cell-background labels v8 (N039): mechanism confirmed (CD19 FOV excess .51 -> .00) but pre-registered QC FAILED (draw-1 CD19 has no positive mode; r(v8,v5) CD19 .53/.69, CD14 draw 1 .925), v8 not used [verified] (N036, N037, N039; .agent-research/results/N037-goal-retrain-on-cross-fitted-labels-n031/n037_goal.csv, .agent-research/results/N036-label-position-detrend-v7-cross-fit-the/fov_share.csv) {cites:0}
- K032: MODEL-SIDE NULLS ON THE GOAL (v5 metric): physics-based LED nuisance augmentation single base .6450 vs .6425 (+.0025; ensemble .6531 vs .6527), +tail05 CD123 +.031 but CD19 -.033 (N041); low-pass sigma 1.5 px input .6411 vs .6425, weak targets <= .011 -> not image-limited, N042 stage 2 killed; ConvNeXt-T member alone .6135, residual r with the family .94-.96, ensemble .6533/.6570 (no gain, N050) -> shared error is label/readout-driven, not model-family [verified] (N041, N042, N050; .agent-research/results/N041-physics-based-source-only-nuisance-rando/scores_goal.csv, .agent-research/results/N042-weak-marker-architecture-low-pass-input/n042_lowpass_per_target.csv, .agent-research/results/N050-heterogeneous-ensemble-member-different/n050_residual_corr.csv) {cites:0}
- K034: NOISE-AWARE POSITIVE/NEGATIVE LABELS ARE NOT IDENTIFIABLE (N049, killed at the fitting stage, no GPU run): labelling efficiency eta and false-positive rate phi are not separable in a two-emission mixture (only q = pi*eta + (1-pi)*phi), so the fit reduces to prior-driven smoothing that zeroes rare positives (draw-2 CD19/HLA-DR targets all 0, red-team reproduced). Correction (N051): the 'cofactor 150 erases CD123+' reading was WRONG (tail contrast 49.5 -> 68.7/76.3); that d'=0 fit was a local optimum. By-product: on cofactor-150 labels positives are separable (CD3 d' 7.4-7.6, CD56 5.5-5.8, CD19 5.2-8.8) [verified] (N049, N051; .agent-research/results/N049-noise-aware-positive-negative-marker-lab/v9fit/, .agent-research/results/N051-label-v10-per-marker-asinh-cofactor-pre/n051_metrics.csv) {cites:0}

### GS chain
- K005: GS<->LF pairs are real: Wright-morphology clusters (DinoBloom k-means) agree with LF-predicted lineage at 0.858 cell level; a PBC-trained classifier collapses on BSCCM Wright cells (72 % "platelet") -> BSCCM GS is far from clinical smears [verified] (N008; N008-external-lineage-anchor-pbc-acevedo-mgg/lineage_anchor.json, gs_cluster_vs_lf.json) {cites:3}
- K006: Binding v0 (frozen sup-LF + frozen DinoBloom-B): GS<->LF exact-cell retrieval near chance on the held-out slide; autofl on real GS cells: LF teacher .61, distilled GS .27, head transfer -.05, direct GS ceiling .37 -> distillation >> head transfer [stale: autofl truth was NOT position-detrended (K007); distillation re-confirmed on detrended truth in K011, head transfer not re-tested] (N009; item text, /hnvme/workspace/v181bb10-bsccm/runs/n009_bind_v0) {cites:2}
- K009: Detrended autofl on GS cells: Wright-image signal transfers across the two stained slides (ridge within .57/.68, cross .55/.47; LF within .56/.76, cross .47/.24) [verified] (N012; N012-skeptic-control-is-the-within-slide-gs-a/spatial_detrend.json) {cites:2}
- K012: Simulated mosaic with ground truth (pseudo-GS = BF+DPC+phase, pivot = 1-17 darkfield patterns): no-assumption bound [(a-b)^2,(a+b)^2] covers 95 % (92-100 % per pivot); CIA estimate a^2+b^2 median rel. error +5..+15 % (conservative); distilled ~= direct oracle (.46-.49 vs .465). Caveat: one instrument, milder CIA violations than real GS [verified] (N016; N016-simulated-mosaic-with-ground-truth-pseud/sim_mosaic.csv) {cites:2}
- K016: Class-anchored alignment (anchors neutrophil/lymphocyte/monocyte only) transfers lineage-level markers to PBC half B (anchored contrasts .79-1.00, 2 seeds; partly circular) and held-out IG/erythroblast contrasts (.83-.98); finer biology is NOT robust: eosinophil CD16-low .95/.36, basophil CD123 .49/.61; +DANN harmful (eos .55, baso .15) [verified] (N021; N021-class-anchored-alignment-to-pbc-anchors/pbc_anchor_auroc.csv) {cites:2}
- K035: SEMI-SUPERVISED OT ALIGNMENT (SOTAlign) IS FLAT/NEGATIVE for Giemsa<->LF (N045, seed 0 screen, GPU v1 + CPU v2): cross-slide exact-cell R@10 sotalign .036/.020 vs pairs-only SigLIP .038/.022 (chance .0018/.0010); transferred autofl r cross sotalign .44/.21 vs raw ridge .65/.46 vs distillation student TT6c .715/.601; PBC-B lineage AUROC .51-.58 vs distilled students .95-1.00; PBC re-centring and 3x steps change nothing. An aligned space finds the same cell (~20x chance) but carries little marker information -> distillation stays the bridge [partial: 1 seed] (N045; .agent-research/results/N045-sotalign-semi-supervised-ot-alignment-gi/v2_summary.csv) {cites:0}

### Clinical transfer and LF teacher (moved from Headline at lint 2026-11-12)
- K015: The BSCCM-trained GS student does NOT transfer to clinical PBC smears: pre-registered lineage AUROCs at chance or inverted (CD16 neut>eos .11, CD45 lym>neut .33; only CD14 .70). Unconditional DANN to unlabelled PBC is unstable (mean .41 -> .46/.56, CD14 .70 -> .26) [verified] (N019, N020; N020-clinical-transfer-via-unsupervised-domai/pbc_transfer_auroc.csv) {cites:3}
- K020: Fine-grained teacher (tail weighting + focal 10 gates) helps in-distribution only (FOV .654 -> .674) and r50 SSL teachers distil WORSE into the Giemsa student than the r18 supervised teacher (MLL23 12 fine contrasts .50/.49 vs .63, 3 seeds); NK-LGL CD56 and basophil CD123 fail in every arm [verified] (N022; .agent-research/results/N022-fine-grained-teacher-rare-population-tai/transfer_multiseed.csv) {cites:1}
- K013: Real GS->MK estimate under CIA, r(GS,M) ~= r(S,T)*r(T,M): CD16 .79/.82, CD45 .78/.44, CD14 .73/.67 > grp CD3/19/56 .70/.43 > CD3 .48/.40, HLA-DR .43/.49 > CD19/CD56/CD123 .03-.21 (b0->b1 / b1->b0) -> Giemsa-visible = lineage markers [partial: grp:CD123/HLA-DR/CD14 batch-1 labels failed QC (N023); estimates using that target are unreliable] (N017; N017-real-gs-mk-error-estimate-without-gs-mk/gs_mk_estimates.csv) {cites:2}
- K014: LF information map (FOV split, v4): every LED group carries most of the signal (BF alone .585 = 92 % of ALL .635); CD123 is darkfield-borne (DF_all .38 ~ ALL .39 vs BF/phase .24); lymphoid/CD45/CD16 groups best from phase-contrast morphology (.83-.84). Batch-held-out map not run [verified] (N018; N018-lf-information-map-supervised-r18-per-le/info_map_fov_v4.csv) {cites:1}
- K010: GOAL best .5742 = SSL(aug)-init r50 fine-tuned 10 ep (b1to0 .571 / b0to1 .577); r50 15 ep .5654; DANN .1 r18 .5541 (flat) vs r18 v4 .5545; gain concentrated in CD123 (+.12-.17), CD19/CD56 (+.05) [verified, LEGACY metric: 12-target v4, unresolved after N023 re-base] (N014; N014-teacher-v4-portfolio-resnet50-x15-ep-ssl/n014_goal.csv, plots/batch-holdout-lf-mk-r-mean-v4_2026-11-09_1228.png) {cites:3}
- K021: [caveat N025 F1: target preprocessing used Giemsa autofl; see N029] Giemsa chain with a v5-label r18 teacher (N024): same-cell autofl truth within-slide .38 -> .51 (batch-0 slide) and .69 -> .87 (batch-1), 3 seeds; cross-slide .32 -> .59, .65 -> .78 (1 seed); BUT MLL23 fine contrasts .62 -> .54 (neutrophil CD16 drops). Pooled two-slide autofl r is NOT comparable across v4/v5 truth (rescaling alone .25 -> .48) -> use within-slide r [partial] (N024; .agent-research/results/N024-v5-label-r18-supervised-teacher-for-the/n024_metrics.csv) {cites:1}
- K022: [N032: clinical numbers are teacher-run dependent (.48-.61), see K025; N029: autofl gain confirmed on clean labels (TT6c .564/.848); clinical .611 not reproduced by retrained teachers (.551) -> teacher-run variance, N032] Two-teacher Giemsa student TT6 (v4-r18 markers + v6-r18 autofl from unstained slides only) improves same-cell autofl truth within-slide .383/.689 -> .578/.855 and substantially recovers MLL23 clinical fine contrasts (.611 vs v4 .622; paired diff -.011, 95 % CI [-.039, +.017]; non-inferiority unproven). MLL23 is a reused development benchmark from N022 on. Caveat: target preprocessing used Giemsa autofl (v3/v4 fits incl. GS rows) -> clean rebuild N029 [partial] (N025; .agent-research/results/N025-giemsa-chain-without-the-trade-off-two-t/n025_metrics.csv) {cites:1}
- K024: Virtual Wright staining from label-free LED images works (N028, UNet + L1/blurred-L1 + DinoBloom loss, 10 min on 1 H100, 12k registered pairs): held-out PSNR 27.7, SSIM .88, exact-cell retrieval 34-84x chance; a Giemsa student reads lineage markers from virtual stains like from real ones (agreement CD45 .95, CD16 .93, CD14/CD3 .90) but loses fine detail (CD123/CD19 ~.5; autofl truth 74-82 % of real). Registration needs unwhitened ZNCC (phase correlation picked random shifts) [partial] (N028; .agent-research/results/N028-virtual-wright-giemsa-staining-from-labe/downstream_tt6s0.json) {cites:1}

### Generative / set-level matching
- K026: SET-LEVEL DISTRIBUTION MATCHING NEEDS SAME-CELL SETS OR VARYING COMPOSITION (N034-B v2): linear readout on frozen SSL LF features (n007, transductive unlabelled pretraining) learnt only from set-level information (bag-mean ridge / 1-D OT), clean v5c labels, new-draw split 2, mean r over 7 targets: paired .561; SAME cells with pairing hidden, random sets of 4/16/64/256/2048: .548/.503/.451/.309/.104 (lineage markers ~97 % at 16, autofl/CD19 50-60 %); DIFFERENT cells of the same slide, random or same-FOV groups: no positive recovery with any learner/size (mean |r| .05-.15 of both signs = FOV-level components, max .48; no permutation null). The first (OT-only) bench understated large same-cell sets (learner failure, red-team N4 reproduced: synthetic OT .03 vs bag-mean .99). Scope: these learners/designs, 1 run, large-n decline partly few-bag regression [partial] (N034; .agent-research/results/N034-lf-fluorescence-marker-images-by-conditi/setmatch/setmatch_sim_v2.csv) {cites:0}
- K027: LF -> FLUORESCENCE IMAGES BY CONDITIONAL FLOW MATCHING (N034-A, 28 M UNet, patch-2, b1->b0, 1 seed): per-cell r needs >= 48 Heun steps + CFG 2-3 (16 steps under-disperse); distribution scores already beat regression at s16 g2 or s48 g1 (s16 g1 wins CRPS only). At s48 g2-3: distributionally better than the same net as regression (DEVELOPMENT numbers, sampler chosen on them; new draw CRPS .57 vs .78, conditional W1 .55 vs .74; rank calibration still fails, outside-fraction .77 vs .40; marginal W1 is passed by an LF-shuffled control, so only conditional scores count), equal per cell on lineage markers (CD16 .86, CD14 .86, CD45 .76) but worse on subtle ones (CD3 .25 vs .55, HLA-DR .36 vs .50; mean .55 vs .61). Image targets: border-median bg, smooth position gain kept only if it generalises to held-out FOVs (72/132; the HGB gain fitted FOV-composition noise) CONFIRMED by the frozen pre-registered reverse-direction test N035 (train draw 0, untouched draw-1 split 1, sampler frozen at s48 g2): CRPS .674 vs .815, condW1 .692 vs .727 (7/12 labels), r .476 vs .576 (worse on all 12), outside .53 vs ideal .22; on a new draw CFG 2 over-disperses (sd ratio 1.25). HLA-DR's real-image readout does not transfer between draws (r -.11) [1 seed per direction, readout yardstick] (N034; .agent-research/results/N034-lf-fluorescence-marker-images-by-conditi/n034_sampler_sweep.csv; N035; .agent-research/results/N035-frozen-confirmation-of-n034-a-in-the-unt/n035_means.csv) {cites:0}

## Refuted
- "The within-slide GS->autofl signal (r .62) is Wright-morphology biology" -- killed by N012: slide position alone predicts autofl on GS cells r .72/.61 (cell-random CV), .59/.57 region-blocked (N012-skeptic-control-is-the-within-slide-gs-a/spatial_control.json). See K007.
- "CD19/CD56/CD123 are not predictable from LF in a new isolation" (v3 held-out CD19 -.05) -- killed by N013: on detrended v4 labels held-out CD19 .28/.32, CD56 .35/.33 (n013_v4_final_evals.json). The v3 within-batch signal was learned slide-position artefact.
- "Stain normalisation (Macenko) or adversarial slide invariance closes the cross-slide GS gap" -- killed by N010/N011: autofl-truth r .284 (aug) / .287 (Macenko) / .304 (Macenko+DANN) / .308 (DANN), all within noise (item text; N011-diagnose-the-cross-slide-gs-failure-auto/macenko_check.png).
- "SSL pretraining does not help LF->MK (weak linear probe, N007)" -- killed by N014: SSL(aug)-init fine-tune is the best teacher, .5742 vs r50 .5654 (n014_goal.csv).
- "Unconditional DANN to unlabelled PBC gives clinical transfer" -- killed by N020: per-contrast AUROCs swing between configs (CD14 .70 -> .26, CD16 neut>lym .49 -> .22 -> .82) (pbc_transfer_auroc.csv); class-anchored alignment (K016) is needed.
- "Procrustes rotation (PRH/shared-latent) transfers GS<->LF better out-of-slide than learned heads" -- killed by N009 zero-training screen: cross-slide Procrustes R@10 .018 vs linear SigLIP .033 (N009-stage-2-binding-v0-on-frozen-sup-lf-feat/screen_B/screen.json).
- K036: PRETRAINED LF ENCODERS (N053): with a learned per-LED gate + 24-channel patch embedding, fine-tuned at encoder lr x0.1, no
  pretrained encoder beats the SSL ResNet-50 alone on the v10 GOAL (r50 .6730; Cytoland VSCyto2D ConvNeXtV2 .6671/.6649 two seeds;
  DinoBloom-B .6552; DINOv3-B .6515; DINOv3-S .6495; Cytoland at full lr .6464). As a third ensemble member Cytoland lifts the
  N048 ensemble .6804 -> .6862 / .6864 (seed 0 / 1) = new GOAL best; best same-size r50-family control .6826, Cytoland-specific
  part +.0036 (FOV-bootstrap CI [.0007, .0062]); its errors correlate least with the r50 family (.91 vs .95-.99) while staying
  accurate; ViT members add nothing (.6803-.6816). All encoders up-weight high-angle darkfield (DF_90/85/80) [verified] (N053;
  .agent-research/results/N053-lf-encoder-swap-on-the-v10-goal-dinov3-v/n053_followup.csv) {cites:0}
- K037: RESIDUAL FLOW MATCHING (N044, CorrDiff-style): flow on (y - mu)/sigma conditioned on LF + frozen regressor mean removes the
  plain flow's per-cell accuracy loss (r_avgread in-batch .692 vs plain .612, new draw .594 vs .550; regressor .695/.599) and
